{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/gold-v1.json | sed -n '199,254p;852,905p'\"","aggregated_output":"   199\t   \"question_id\": \"q04\",\n   200\t   \"question\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?\",\n   201\t   \"kind\": \"theme\",\n   202\t   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   203\t   \"seed_view_id\": \"v4\",\n   204\t   \"source\": \"reader B\",\n   205\t   \"no_view\": false,\n   206\t   \"reference\": {\n   207\t    \"text\": \"The big four's own plans: around $650bn this year (i256, i089, i253), the figure NVIDIA management also cites (i173).\",\n   208\t    \"value\": 650000000000,\n   209\t    \"items\": [\n   210\t     \"i256\",\n   211\t     \"i089\",\n   212\t     \"i173\",\n   213\t     \"i253\"\n   214\t    ]\n   215\t   },\n   216\t   \"implied_outcome\": {\n   217\t    \"text\": \"Alphabet alone guides up to $190bn (i232); Google Cloud backlog nearly doubled to over $460bn (i233) and Microsoft's remaining performance obligations are $627bn (i039), so plans drift up rather than down; memory prices sharply higher and tight until 2028 (i252, i143) lift the dollar cost of the same build; NVIDIA reports accelerating growth (i295) and SemiAnalysis sees second-half shipments above market estimates (i111). Against that, more than 75 US projects worth about $130bn have been blocked or delayed this year (i146, i041). I bet $650-720bn.\",\n   218\t    \"low\": 650000000000,\n   219\t    \"high\": 720000000000,\n   220\t    \"yes_no\": null,\n   221\t    \"items\": [\n   222\t     \"i232\",\n   223\t     \"i233\",\n   224\t     \"i039\",\n   225\t     \"i252\",\n   226\t     \"i295\",\n   227\t     \"i111\",\n   228\t     \"i146\"\n   229\t    ]\n   230\t   },\n   231\t   \"direction\": \"in_line\",\n   232\t   \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n   233\t   \"decisive_items\": [\n   234\t    \"i256\",\n   235\t    \"i232\",\n   236\t    \"i233\",\n   237\t    \"i295\"\n   238\t   ],\n   239\t   \"against\": {\n   240\t    \"text\": \"Local opposition has blocked or delayed more than 75 US data-center projects worth about $130bn so far this year (i146, i041), and Meta's CEO has spoken of slower-than-expected progress in AI agents (i292).\",\n   241\t    \"items\": [\n   242\t     \"i146\",\n   243\t     \"i292\"\n   244\t    ]\n   245\t   },\n   246\t   \"reasoning\": \"The big four's own plans are around $650bn for 2026 (i256, i089, i253), and NVIDIA management uses the same figure (i173). Alphabet guides up to $190bn (i232), Google Cloud's backlog nearly doubled to over $460bn (i233) and Microsoft's remaining performance obligations are $627bn (i039), so the contracted demand behind the plans is growing, and memory prices sharply higher and tight until 2028 (i252, i143) raise the dollar cost of the same build. NVIDIA reports accelerating growth as it nears $100bn quarters (i295) and SemiAnalysis sees second-half shipments above market estimates (i111), which is what the hyperscalers' cheques pay for. Against that, more than 75 US data-center projects worth about $130bn have been blocked or delayed this year (i146, i041), and Meta's CEO has spoken of slower-than-expected AI-agent progress (i292). I bet $650-720bn: in line with the plan, with the drift upward.\"\n   247\t  },\n   248\t  {\n   249\t   \"question_id\": \"q05\",\n   250\t   \"question\": \"How will server DRAM and HBM contract prices in calendar 2027 compare with calendar 2026?\",\n   251\t   \"kind\": \"theme\",\n   252\t   \"unit\": \"percent change 2027 vs 2026 (10 means up 10%)\",\n   253\t   \"seed_view_id\": \"v5\",\n   254\t   \"source\": \"reader B\",\n   852\t   \"question_id\": \"q19\",\n   853\t   \"question\": \"How much revenue will NVIDIA report from standalone Vera CPUs in FY2027?\",\n   854\t   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   855\t   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   856\t   \"seed_view_id\": \"v19\",\n   857\t   \"source\": \"reader B\",\n   858\t   \"no_view\": false,\n   859\t   \"reference\": {\n   860\t    \"text\": \"Management's own figure: $20bn of stand-alone CPU sales this year (i095), by the end of this fiscal year (i288), nearly $20bn with no period (i080): one claim retold three times.\",\n   861\t    \"value\": 20000000000,\n   862\t    \"items\": [\n   863\t     \"i288\",\n   864\t     \"i095\",\n   865\t     \"i080\"\n   866\t    ]\n   867\t   },\n   868\t   \"implied_outcome\": {\n   869\t    \"text\": \"The first stand-alone CPU launches this fall (i096), so the revenue falls in roughly two quarters; at Morgan Stanley's $5,000 per Vera CPU (i218), $20bn is four million units. Demand signals are real: Perplexity plans to deploy Vera in production (i262, i291) and Intel's CEO sees the CPU:GPU ratio in inference moving toward 1:1 (i009); but NVIDIA chose Intel Xeon 6 as host CPU for DGX Rubin NVL8 (i008). I bet $8-18bn, below the $20bn ambition.\",\n   870\t    \"low\": 8000000000,\n   871\t    \"high\": 18000000000,\n   872\t    \"yes_no\": null,\n   873\t    \"items\": [\n   874\t     \"i096\",\n   875\t     \"i218\",\n   876\t     \"i262\",\n   877\t     \"i291\",\n   878\t     \"i009\",\n   879\t     \"i008\"\n   880\t    ]\n   881\t   },\n   882\t   \"direction\": \"below\",\n   883\t   \"confidence\": \"low\",\n   884\t   \"decisive_items\": [\n   885\t    \"i288\",\n   886\t    \"i095\",\n   887\t    \"i096\",\n   888\t    \"i218\"\n   889\t   ],\n   890\t   \"against\": {\n   891\t    \"text\": \"Management expects $20bn by fiscal year-end (i288, i095), and Intel's CEO describes inference moving toward one CPU per GPU (i009).\",\n   892\t    \"items\": [\n   893\t     \"i288\",\n   894\t     \"i009\"\n   895\t    ]\n   896\t   },\n   897\t   \"reasoning\": \"The reference is management's own number: $20bn of stand-alone CPU sales this year (i095), by the end of this fiscal year (i288), nearly $20bn with no period (i080), one claim retold three times. The first stand-alone CPU launches this fall (i096), so the revenue falls in roughly two quarters, and at Morgan Stanley's $5,000 per Vera CPU (i218) $20bn is four million units. Demand signals are real: Perplexity plans to deploy Vera in production after a 1.5x result on agentic coding (i262, i291), and Intel's CEO sees the CPU:GPU ratio in inference moving from 1:8 toward 1:1 (i009); but NVIDIA itself chose Intel Xeon 6 as host CPU for DGX Rubin NVL8 (i008). Lean cautious on a product with no shipments yet: I bet $8-18bn, below the $20bn ambition, with the top of the range reachable if the fall ramp is steep. Management's $20bn (i288, i095) is the strongest item against.\"\n   898\t  },\n   899\t  {\n   900\t   \"question_id\": \"q20\",\n   901\t   \"question\": \"How much revenue will NVIDIA report from Blackwell and Rubin products in FY2027?\",\n   902\t   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   903\t   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   904\t   \"seed_view_id\": \"v20\",\n   905\t   \"source\": \"reader B\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md | sed -n '162,190p;316,395p'\"","aggregated_output":"   162\t## 5. The $0 blind test (registered; REPAIR-DESIGN.md §5 with rounds 51's fixes)\n   163\t\n   164\t**Inputs.** Each case's archive, call, question, ladder and unit are registered, and the build refuses a heading that differs.\n   165\t\n   166\t| Case | Archive / call | Key | Ladder edges ($bn) | Role |\n   167\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n   168\t| P (joint), P-v4, P-v8 (separate) | old-1 v4 8810, v8 8816 | NVIDIA revenue company FY2027; NVIDIA revenue Data Center FY2027 | 431.2/392/352.8/313.6; 400/350/300/250 | the pair; 79 quotes absent from the gate |\n   169\t| S | old-3 v6 9043 | four largest AI hyperscalers, data-center capex, combined, CY2026 | 500/600/700/800 | fresh: 41 of 50 quotes absent from the gate |\n   170\t| O | old-2 v29 8507 | NVIDIA equity investment commitments company end of FY2027 (the fiscal year-end balance the annual report publishes) | 25/50/75/100 | control |\n   171\t| E | old-3 v41 9071 | NVIDIA revenue Vera CPU FY2028 | 50/40/30/20 | control |\n   172\t\n   173\t**Part A, code, $0.** Each case asserts its intended rule and message. The schema's validity is checked first, so a schema error\n   174\tcannot mask the rule under test.\n   175\t- **A1, correct forms.** Each passes:\n   176\t  - a $4.5 billion ± 3% guidance as two sources with apply_growth ends;\n   177\t  - Q1 + Q2 = H1;\n   178\t  - FY − Q1-Q3 = Q4;\n   179\t  - a year-over-year rate on last year's quarter (recorded);\n   180\t  - whole × mix through share;\n   181\t  - \"over $300 billion\" with qualifier over;\n   182\t  - \"-3%\";\n   183\t  - \"$300 million or more\" with qualifier \"or more\";\n   184\t  - $1.2 trillion as 1200 USD bn;\n   185\t  - a range outcome overlapping its rung;\n   186\t  - one figure marked for two members (its own family);\n   187\t  - a computed external reference;\n   188\t  - an unresolved member;\n   189\t  - a conversion between quantities (recorded);\n   190\t  - \"not only still expects $20 billion\" as a source;\n   316\t- **Blinding.** 14 packets under a fresh shuffle (ids Q01–Q14, key in `reread-key.json` beside, never in the packets). The readers are\n   317\t  fresh: one Claude subagent and one Codex session per packet. They see only their packet, never earlier votes, the key or the expected\n   318\t  result.\n   319\t- **Scoring:**\n   320\t  - The registered stop lines apply to the 12 replies exactly as before, with adjudication where the readers disagree.\n   321\t  - The repair fails if either control is read wrongly by both readers, or by the adjudication when the two readers split on it.\n   322\t  - Any registered stop on the 12 replies, including S losing its only usable reply, sends the result back to council.\n   323\t  - A clean re-read goes to Alex for the paid re-send, beside the third run's record and its disclosures.\n   324\t\n   325\t**[D744] The second blinded re-read (Alex: \"批准再重读一次\"; council round 58), registered before any packet is built.**\n   326\t- **The one change: shared rule text.** Readers get the same rule material as adjudicators, from one source (`blind_rules.py`): the\n   327\t  writer's system text, every schema description, and the definitions, which allow what the format rules permit. Readers judge in two\n   328\t  steps:\n   329\t  1. check quotes and calculations against the format rules;\n   330\t  2. name the evidence for the assumption that sets the band.\n   331\t- **What is re-read.** The same 12 first replies, by fresh readers (one Claude subagent and one Codex session per packet), under a fresh\n   332\t  shuffle T01–T17. The key, with answer paths, is in `reread2-key.json`, never in a packet.\n   333\t- **Five controls**, each checked by the code before use (`blind_reread2.py`), with these expected readings:\n   334\t\n   335\t  | Control | Built from | Expected reading |\n   336\t  |---|---|---|\n   337\t  | K-midpoint | P's Claude reply, guidance given as the midpoint 108 | no \"number misread\" on that figure |\n   338\t  | K-misread | the same reply, guidance given as 108.5 | \"number misread\" on that figure |\n   339\t  | K-overlap | E's Claude reply with a growth range ($36–43B) and consistent text, rung 3 with its reason | no \"broken structure\" |\n   340\t  | K-disjoint | the same reply, rung 4 | \"broken structure\" |\n   341\t  | K-unsupported | E's Claude reply, 140% growth that its own reasons argue against | supported = no |\n   342\t- **Scoring:**\n   343\t  - A control fails if both readers read it wrongly, or, when the readers split on its mark, if the adjudication does.\n   344\t  - The registered stop lines apply to the 12 replies as before, with adjudication where readers disagree. The adjudication packet now\n   345\t    resolves control answers through the key.\n   346\t  - Any failed control or any registered stop ends the re-read, and the result goes back to council.\n   347\t  - Both S replies' support votes and reasons are reported beside the verdict.\n   348\t  - A clean result goes to Alex for the paid re-send.\n   349\t\n   350\t**[D745] The targeted test (Alex: \"批准针对性小测\"; a justified unresolved answer counts as usable, \"算合格\"; council rounds 59–60), registered\n   351\tbefore anything is sent.**\n   352\t- **Request changes** (`judging-v13s.txt`; the v13 request is untouched, its plan hash is unchanged):\n   353\t  - \"If the chosen rung depends on a share, deduction or discount, show what in the passages supports its size or gives a bound that\n   354\t    justifies the rung. If the evidence cannot support a forecast, answer unresolved and explain the gap.\" This replaces the former\n   355\t    unresolved sentence.\n   356\t  - \"discounted by default\" becomes \"discounted subject to the evidence requirement below\".\n   357\t  - The qualifier list adds \"estimated\" (cases 111 of 111, mutants 43 of 43, rehearsal 19 of 19).\n   358\t- **Readers.** Shared rule text (`blind_rules.py`), including the allowed qualifier values and the unresolved ruling. First readers'\n   359\t  step 2 asks:\n   360\t  - for a forecast, the evidence for the band-deciding assumption;\n   361\t  - for an unresolved answer, the gap left after the strongest passages.\n   362\t  Adjudicators get the same definitions.\n   363\t- **Scope** (`blind4.py`; run folder `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/`):\n   364\t  - cases S, E and P-v8;\n   365\t  - 6 unedited first replies (a fresh Claude subagent and a fresh read-only Codex session per case);\n   366\t  - 9 blinded packets (6 replies + 3 controls), each read by one Claude and one Codex reader: 18 first readings, plus adjudication\n   367\t    where they disagree.\n   368\t- **Controls**, each checked by the code before use:\n   369\t\n   370\t  | Control | Built from | Expected reading |\n   371\t  |---|---|---|\n   372\t  | K-unsupported | the saved third-run E Codex reply, with an unsized 15% cut | not supported |\n   373\t  | K-unresolved-unjustified | P-v8 Claude made unresolved with a vague reason | not supported |\n   374\t  | K-unresolved-justified | S made unresolved with the specific gap | supported |\n   375\t- **Pass:**\n   376\t  - every S and E reply has a settled \"yes\" on its forecast or on its reason for leaving the answer unresolved;\n   377\t  - both P-v8 replies have a settled \"yes\" on a forecast;\n   378\t  - all three controls read as expected;\n   379\t  - the refusal and defect stop lines hold as before.\n   380\t- **Otherwise:**\n   381\t  - a support split that adjudication does not settle leaves the run inconclusive, and it goes back to council;\n   382\t  - any failure goes back to council;\n   383\t  - a clean result supports asking Alex to authorize the 36-request paid re-send.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md | sed -n '1,42p;252,300p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# judging-v13 paid gate: plan, harness and reading rule (registered before any send; D725, D729, D730)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Result (D733): STOP.** All 72 answers were refused, and $0.3677 was spent; see `PAID-GATE-RESULT.md`.\n     4\t\n     5\t## 1. What is sent\n     6\t\n     7\t`paid_gate.py plan paid-plan.json` builds 12 requests from the stored runs.\n     8\t\n     9\t| Unit | Arm | Members | Evidence shown |\n    10\t|---|---|---|---|\n    11\t| pair-old-1 (09-20: v4 total, v8 Data Center) | joint; separate-v4; separate-v8 | both; one; one | the union of both stored requests' evidence in view (237 items), in every arm |\n    12\t| pair-old-2 (v14, v9) | joint; separate-v14; separate-v9 | as above | 237 |\n    13\t| pair-old-3 (v3, v35) | joint; separate-v3; separate-v35 | as above | 260 |\n    14\t| single-O (old-2 v29, equity commitments) | single | v29 | its own request's (35) |\n    15\t| single-S (old-2 v6, four hyperscalers' 2027 capex) | single | v6 | 31 |\n    16\t| single-E (old-3 v41, FY2028 Vera CPU) | single | v41 | 15 |\n    17\t\n    18\t- **Each request:** judging-v13's system text (`judging-v13-draft.txt`, 4,373 characters); the family header with the exact outcome\n    19\t  keys; the evidence; the themes once. No earlier forecast is shown (D728). The strict v13 schema.\n    20\t- **The model:** poc-v118's re-judging setting (gpt-6-luna, medium effort, 16,000 output tokens).\n    21\t- **Draws:** three per request, so 36 first attempts.\n    22\t- **Retry:** a calculation the checks refuse, or a schema-invalid answer, is retried once with the reasons. A second refusal makes the\n    23\t  unit unresolved.\n    24\t- **What is scored:** the first attempt, on both arms (§3f). Retries are sent and recorded for diagnosis only.\n    25\t- **The separate arm:** its two first answers per pair and draw are merged and checked over the pair's family (C3, C4 across the two).\n    26\t\n    27\t## 2. Spend and stops\n    28\t\n    29\t- **The ledger:** one, at Alex's ceiling (`paid_gate.py send <folder> <ceiling> paid-plan.json` refuses any other ceiling).\n    30\t- **Budget:** the real budget transport and stop gate, which reserve each request's worst case before sending. After a stop, nothing\n    31\t  more is sent, and the remaining units are recorded as not sent.\n    32\t- **Estimate** (at `hivemind.model.PRICES`: gpt-6-luna, $0.10 input and $0.50 output per million tokens; tokens estimated as\n    33\t  characters / 4):\n    34\t  - a pair request is about 34–38k input tokens and a singleton 6–9k;\n    35\t  - the 36 first attempts cost about $0.17 at 4,000 output tokens each, and at most $0.39 if every answer used its 16,000-token cap;\n    36\t  - the transport reserves at most $0.039 for one request.\n    37\t  - **Proposed ceiling: $0.50.** It covers every scored attempt. Retries come last (§3g), so a ceiling stop among them leaves the\n    38\t    scored test complete.\n    39\t- **Sends:** one at a time, every first attempt before any retry (§3g). Each send has its own archive, so no draw is answered from\n    40\t  another.\n    41\t\n    42\t## 3. The $0 rehearsal (`paid_rehearsal.py`, `rehearsal.log`: 16 of 16)\n   252\t## 4. The reading rule (fixed now, before any answer exists)\n   253\t\n   254\t- **Packets:** 27 (`paid_gate.py packets`): 9 joint pair-draws, 9 reconciled separate pair-draws and 9 singleton draws. The labels are\n   255\t  shuffled, the arm is hidden, and the key is kept in `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/`.\n   256\t  - Each packet shows, per card (K1, K2), the question, the ladder, every passage the final answer names (as the request showed it),\n   257\t    its figures, the recomputed outcome, the recorded assumptions and the card. Nothing about attempts or the code's decision is\n   258\t    shown (§3e).\n   259\t  - A packet the code did not publish (held, unresolved, not reconciled) is read too. The verdict, not the reader, applies the code's\n   260\t    decision: its cards cannot count as usable.\n   261\t  - The readers receive `packets.md` exactly, with its key-commitment line. The readings file carries that text's sha256.\n   262\t- **Readers:** two fresh readers of different families, a Codex session and a Claude subagent, each blind to the other and to the arm.\n   263\t  For each card each answers four questions, yes or no, with the passage that decides:\n   264\t  1. **usable:** the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on;\n   265\t  2. **contradiction:** with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction;\n   266\t  3. **internal_reference:** the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation;\n   267\t  4. **deciding_gap:** an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band.\n   268\t- **Agreement:** where the two readers agree, that is the reading. Where they disagree, a third fresh reader (Codex) reads the card with\n   269\t  both readings and the passages, and its answer decides. No reading is changed after the verdict is computed.\n   270\t- **Verdict** (`paid_gate.py verdict`, D725's lines, on the first attempts; computed once and sealed, §3f):\n   271\t  - **PASS:** the joint arm has both cards usable in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot, and at least 3 more usable\n   272\t    pairs than the separate arm; and zero published defects (contradiction, internal reference or deciding gap) across the joint and\n   273\t    singleton answers.\n   274\t  - **STOP:** any such published defect; a coverage line missed; a gain under 3.\n   275\t  - **INCOMPLETE:** a packet or a card missing a reading, or a unit not sent.\n   276\t  - This is a small design test, not release acceptance.\n   277\t\n   278\t## 5. What the result decides\n   279\t\n   280\t- **PASS:** judging-v13 earns a production design: automatic families in matching, lifecycle and the request builder, each a further\n   281\t  step Alex opens.\n   282\t- **STOP or INCOMPLETE:** the line goes back to Alex with the readings, and nothing is tuned on these 36 answers.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '59,90p;326,418p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '59,90p;326,418p'\"","aggregated_output":"    59\t## 1. Before acting on a failure: diagnose\n    60\t\n    61\tA failure is a question, not a task. Nothing changes (code, prompt, configuration, test, gold) until these are written:\n    62\t\n    63\t1. **The class.** Count every instance on stored data, at no cost: how many, since when, what each costs; never only the case in view.\n    64\t   Match by path or field, not by substring, and check the census on one case whose answer is known. A flagged word in a document is a\n    65\t   class too: count it over the whole scope before the first edit.\n    66\t2. **The mechanism.** Trace one case end to end (the raw output, every check that dropped it, the input that produced it, the code\n    67\t   that built that input) to the design choice that produces the whole class. First check whether your own last change or load caused\n    68\t   it; when several mechanisms stack on the same cases, find them all first.\n    69\t3. **Step back.** Is it the product's problem, or one the measurement or process made? Read the governing standard and the decisions on\n    70\t   the topic before writing any rule: the answer is often written already, and a question about the measuring stick is answered by the\n    71\t   frozen ruler (§7.1), never by a new ruler (Alex, 2026-10-29: \"我们是聊过这个事情的你难道没看文档吗\").\n    72\t4. **The cheapest proof.** Show the change flips the decisive case on real data (a stored input edited and re-run, a rule run on a copy\n    73\t   of stored data) and count what else it fires or touches. If it does not flip, the cause is elsewhere: trace again and build nothing.\n    74\t5. **The share.** Show what share of the counted class the fix removes. A fix that removes part of it is a patch: say so, and do not\n    75\t   build it as the fix. A fix that another change subsumes is not built.\n    76\t\n    77\tBefore any design: ten raw answers read beside their inputs, the whole request read as the model reads it, and, for a choice the model\n    78\tmade, the model's own account (continue the stored conversation with \"which instruction led you here, and which two statements did you\n    79\treject\", a cent a case).\n    80\t\n    81\tThen converge or stop:\n    82\t- A mechanism named on its counted class is fixed in the same slice and measured, and the report leads with it. A root-caused defect is\n    83\t  never parked \"for Alex\"; a parked fix is an open defect. Go to Alex only when the mechanism is not found, or the fix would change the\n    84\t  measuring stick or the PRD.\n    85\t- When one mechanism draws findings round after round, stop answering findings: propose one structural rule.\n    86\t- A failure called a flake is a defect until traced. Read a failing check to its first differing line before any rerun; a passing rerun\n    87\t  proves nothing.\n    88\t- A subagent's or reviewer's report is a lead. Read the code, contract or record it rests on before acting on it or recording it, and\n    89\t  cite what you read, not the summary (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"那你找到的这些问题验证是真的问题吗？\").\n    90\t\n   326\t### 7.3 Iterating\n   327\t\n   328\t- **One class at a time** (Alex, 2026-10-29: \"你一类一类改，快速迭代然后测regression\"). Count the misses by mechanism; take the largest\n   329\t  class; trace it to the sentence that causes it; change one thing aimed at that class; run the whole bench (a prompt change alters every\n   330\t  request) against the previous version; read every regression to its raw answer. The pages that showed the failure locate its\n   331\t  mechanism; only the whole bench (every set, every draw) accepts the change.\n   332\t- **Name the effect on the judgement first.** Every proposed change states the effect it is expected to have on a reader or on the final\n   333\t  judgement, and is tested there where possible; a step's own counts do not decide it alone. A fix that keeps moving its error to\n   334\t  neighbouring cases stops being tuned on that set (Alex, 2026-11-09: \"感觉现在一直在修一些mknor的原地打转，你是不是要思考下现在具体还差什么high priority big impact 的需要做？\";\n   335\t  he approved this rule the same day, D391).\n   336\t- **A model call is a sampler.** Re-send a stored request before calling its answer a defect. Totals and acceptance come from at least\n   337\t  three samples beside a fresh control; a bar the control fails against itself judges nothing. A direct-read pass\n   338\t  (one send per article, every answer read beside its source; D238) locates mechanisms; its counts are one draw and are labelled so.\n   339\t- **A written log.** One row per arm: hypothesis, change, numbers against the control (regressions first), kept or not. Refuted arms and\n   340\t  your own mistakes stay in it; the next session starts from its last row.\n   341\t- **Own the loop, within what Alex agreed.** When the direction is agreed and no stop is in force (`CURRENT_STATE.md`), push your own\n   342\t  hypotheses through $0 checks and probes of a few cents on stored cases without asking. A registered test, an end-to-end run, or\n   343\t  anything that departs from the agreed plan starts on his word; a result that contradicts the hypothesis stops the line and goes to him\n   344\t  (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\"). While he is not active (D439), \"his word\" is the council's\n   345\t  recorded consensus, and a stopped line goes to the council for re-assessment.\n   346\t- **Council before every change is sent.** A prompt, schema, code or criterion change, including one found by reading a probe, is a new\n   347\t  arm. It goes to an independent Codex read and a challenge round before its first send, and its result goes to a challenge round\n   348\t  before the next change. Reading the traces and the model's own account locates a fix; it does not review it (Alex, 2026-11-08:\n   349\t  \"你这些改动有我你有好好的跑council 再下手\").\n   350\t  Every round's reasoning and decisions are reflected on in the council until there is a consensus; the decision is recorded, and\n   351\t  the next test goes straight ahead, held to the PRD and its quantified goals, with every trace read by you yourself and not only\n   352\t  by readers (Alex, 2026-11-10: \"你应该跑council loop 来reflect 你每一轮的思路还有决策，需要你打成共识，记录决策，向前直行测试。不要drift,我们有PRD和量化目标，\n   353\t  你自己作为llm 下去看所有trace\").\n   354\t- **Small first, then one run.** A hypothesis is first validated the simplest way, on a few stored cases and a few cents, and shown to\n   355\t  work at a high level before any full analysis or stability test is built (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"don't overspend resources on wasting time.\n   356\t  We need to validate the hypothesis in a very simple way and to make sure that it works on a high level before we dive into do the full\n   357\t  analysis stability test. This is a principle you should remember\"). A day or week slice before any whole-corpus run; preflight on\n   358\t  stored data before any paid run (§5); no edit while a run is live (§9). A paid run measures a configuration; it never tries a fix.\n   359\t  Before each send, write what it can still change in the decision and which risk the cheaper check left uncovered; a replicate or\n   360\t  control that only re-measures noise or a settled comparison is not sent, and a fix is not sent before the model's own account and the\n   361\t  request locate where the decision is made (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"你跑这么多次真的有意义吗\"; \"我感觉你在为了跑而跑\"). Several fixes on one\n   362\t  base are each proved on stored data in minutes and then run together once (Alex, 2026-11-02: \"快速验证。不要drift,不要跑超级繁琐的全方位验证，先poc 改，能work,有结论，全部改动放到一起再跑完整\"; D266).\n   363\t- **One recommendation, one test.** What reaches Alex as the next step of work is one recommendation and one test of it, reached after\n   364\t  rounds of review (Claude's own, Codex's, an independent reader's) on the traces until a round finds nothing serious; never a menu of\n   365\t  arms or options, never a conclusion the next probe overturns (a choice that changes what the system does still goes to him with its\n   366\t  options and a recommendation, Authority and scope) (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"就测试一种，一次 … 你就没有自己看5轮review，能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议？\").\n   367\t  An agreed recommendation is first challenged by an independent reader on the concrete evidence behind it (\"why you give\n   368\t  recommendations for this. What did you see exactly?\"). A review round reads a rule as its author meant it; only a send shows how the\n   369\t  model applies it: before a registered test, the changed request is sent on the cases that motivated it, a few cents.\n   370\t- **A failed arm is diagnosed before the next one.** When an arm fixes its class and regresses another, write the root cause first: the\n   371\t  process error (what grew, what the small sample did not guard) and the mechanism, traced to the raw answers and the model's account,\n   372\t  never a guess stated as the cause. A small sample guards every class the change can move, not only its own. When a fix keeps moving\n   373\t  another class, the call is doing several jobs: move the rule to its owner (a field's definition sits in the schema beside the field)\n   374\t  rather than add a sentence (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"那你这些修改都是失败的呀，为什么，根因，你要检讨然后再接着尝试。我觉得你已经陷入deep loop 了\").\n   375\t  A failed step of a plan is fixed and re-run at that same step: its failures are the work list, and nothing later in the plan and no\n   376\t  substitute plan starts before it passes (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"你为什么要drift? 你现在明明还有这么多的问题要fix,你到底知不知道你要fix什么？\").\n   377\t  Before a fix is proposed, write which goal the mechanism still serves and what the product already gives for it; a measurement that\n   378\t  removes the reason a mechanism exists retires the mechanism instead of starting its repair (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"I told you to think about\n   379\t  it and you're giving me suggestions that you reject yourself\").\n   380\t- **Before a version is rejected, the rejection is checked.** Every failed or refused answer behind a \"did not pass\" is read against its\n   381\t  source and put down as the model's error or the measuring rule's or check's error; a rule or check that refuses right answers is fixed,\n   382\t  and a version that already meets the goal (what it was built to fix is fixed, nothing that was right turned wrong) is not dropped for a\n   383\t  stricter rule a later review added. Alex, 2026-11-05: \"你到底是不是再搬石头砸自己的脚？各种reject自己，你确定是正确的rejection 吗？你又下去看trace吗？\";\n   384\t  \"你不能每次都这样判错然后浪费我时间，我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信下一步你要跑什么才能收敛\".\n   385\t- **Correct, then cheap.** Make the pipeline right and stable before any cost, speed or throughput work; report cost as a baseline only\n   386\t  (Alex, 2026-10-25).\n   387\t\n   388\t## 8. Product thinking\n   389\t\n   390\t- Think like a hedge-fund analyst. A thesis is an argued view about the business and the world; its stance comes from the argument\n   391\t  weighed against what is priced. Extract the few metrics or segments that carry it; financial-statement lines are its evidence, never its\n   392\t  definition.\n   393\t- **Lean cautious, catch the increment.** Most of what an item says is noise: not everything is evidence and not everything is a lead. A\n   394\t  typical claim or background line is common knowledge (what an analyst following the company knew before the item) and is not kept\n   395\t  without a number and a specific narrative; new information that changes an answer is never missed. Alex, 2026-10-29 (D243):\n   396\t  \"不是什么事情都是惊弓之鸟需要抽取，杂音还是很大的，我们整体应该倾向谨慎不要看什么都是线索的感觉，但是同时我们要敏感一些新的信息带来的增量不要错过\".\n   397\t- **A senior analyst's granularity.** A question is a bet an analyst would hold a card for: a big matter, never trivia (a deal, product or\n   398\t  project opens one only when its scale can change revenue, profit, cash or credit risk). Small matters open no question, and whether\n   399\t  their statements are kept follows the evidence rule; wordings, deadlines, milestones and periods of one bet are one question, and a\n   400\t  statement carried by several outlets is one statement (how code applies it: §3, Identity). Two questions stay apart only when their answers can move apart and an analyst\n   401\t  would bet on each separately (D248). Alex, 2026-10-30: \"我觉得核心就是这个颗粒度的把控要符合一个高端的hedge fund analyst 的思维。不要搜集一堆鸡毛蒜皮的事情，要看重要的大事，合并整合关键的信息，这个是这个步骤的原则\".\n   402\t- The extraction standard (§7.1, piece 1) is the step's standard. Its two sources are applied before designing a prompt, evaluation or\n   403\t  change (D228): the thesis library's four evidence tiers (`docs/prd/06-views.md`, Four evidence tiers) and the investment-question\n   404\t  reasoning in the 90-thesis review (`research_notes/对冲基金论点粒度与金标/codex-challenger.md`, section 1; research, not a replacement for\n   405\t  recorded decisions). Source type and what a claim can support are separate judgments; no tier has a fixed score. Ask what revenue,\n   406\t  profitability, cash risk or competitive position the information can change; then separately decide whether it supports an existing\n   407\t  question or merits a new one. Indirect, incomplete and forecast information is evidence under the routing rules; none of those\n   408\t  properties, nor an inability to open a new question, alone makes it worthless.\n   409\t- Evaluate the overall research judgment against the source, the existing question and the evidence. Gold examples teach the reasoning\n   410\t  and its boundaries; reasonable alternative wording, evidence strength and inference are allowed (D226, D228). Record material factual\n   411\t  errors, unsupported assumptions and downstream losses separately. Do not turn a review's questions, output labels or optional details\n   412\t  into an automatic all-or-nothing score. Missing market expectations or historical context means that aspect was not tested, not that\n   413\t  it passed or failed.\n   414\t- When a thesis-quality check fails, look first at the unit of thought (are these the arguments that move the stock?), not deeper into\n   415\t  the numbers. Numbers are verified by code where they exist.\n   416\t- Outcomes are tracked and shown, never a gate on what a view may say. Missing data is \"no data to verify\", never a pass or a fail. A\n   417\t  repeat is not new evidence, and model agreement is not corroboration.\n   418\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
