{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10007,10034p;10957,11003p;11346,11400p;11484,11530p'\"","aggregated_output":" 10007\t## D676 · 2026-11-19 · The release comparison: the new system loses for two known mechanisms; keep the old system; the outcome was computable before the run (council consensus)\n 10008\t\n 10009\t- **Alex:** \"did you measure wrong or what … you go deep into the entire trace and logic and run council loop to reason on this\n 10010\t  comparison and the runs of the two system\".\n 10011\t- **Council:**\n 10012\t  - an independent cold Codex read (`docs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/council-a-codex.md`);\n 10013\t  - Claude's reflection, written first (`claude-reflection.md`);\n 10014\t  - one challenge round (`council-b-codex.md`).\n 10015\t- **Agreed:**\n 10016\t  - **The measurement is sound for the products as configured.**\n 10017\t    - The matter list was built blind from the articles.\n 10018\t    - The mapping was blind with third readers.\n 10019\t    - The controls pass, 13 of 13.\n 10020\t    - The old system's served cards hold on the ones read.\n 10021\t    - No new question was mapped out wrongly.\n 10022\t    - Codex found the old system's Anthropic serve generous; without it b is 6 or 7, still a loss.\n 10023\t  - **Mechanism 1, by design (D382, D384, D505):** the company's own figures are not questions. 7 of the 32 matters are such figures,\n 10024\t    and the old system serves 4 to 6 of them. By D384, five other companies' standalone figures are also outside the new system's\n 10025\t    rules, so its ceiling is 20 of 32 matters.\n 10026\t  - **Mechanism 2, a hand-off defect known since D432:**\n 10027\t    - Step 1 opens bundled questions (two years, or several outcomes), and the frozen ladder refuses them. new-2 lost 27 of 60 and new-3\n 10028\t      19 of 60.\n 10029\t    - Among them are four-hyperscaler capex (M04) and the Anthropic investment (M17) in both runs, and Hugging Face (M19) in new-2.\n 10030\t    - The judge uses pass 1's ladders; new-3's capex question got a valid ladder only on pass 3.\n 10031\t  - **The ceiling ($0 check):** with every dropped key-matter question repaired and served, new is 5–6 against old 10, a = 0, b = 4–5:\n 10032\t    no practical winner, never a lead. Only NVIDIA's own figures (M06, M10, M11, M18) remain.\n 10033\t  - **Process failure:** the attainable verdict was computable in minutes before the run, from the frozen list, D505, D432 and the D489\n 10034\t    week. Neither the council (D665–D667) nor Claude computed it (AGENTS §7.2); two days and about $145 measured a knowable result.\n 10957\t## D725 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 45/45b: the number answers fail because related numbers have no shared, checked calculation; one judge version and one test recommended to Alex\n 10958\t\n 10959\t- **Alex's words** (2026-11-22): \"work with counsel and have a look at the traces of this problem … what is wrong with the system design\n 10960\t  overall … look at the code, look at the traces, deeply battle it out with counsel … because I think it's the most important thing\n 10961\t  that we don't hallucinate with the numbers, and I want you to get this right\".\n 10962\t- **The record:** `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/` (`RESULT.md`).\n 10963\t  - Claude's reflection was written before Codex's.\n 10964\t  - Codex ran an independent investigation (fresh thread `01a20501…`) and a challenge round.\n 10965\t  - Consensus. One wording point stays open: the $146B is arithmetically a residual, but the order of the judge's choices is unknown.\n 10966\t- **Diagnosis:**\n 10967\t  1. Answers are prose; code ties no figure to a source and recomputes nothing. The production check passes contradictory or invented\n 10968\t     figures.\n 10969\t  2. Related questions compute the same quantities separately. The unit is one question, with 0 dependencies.\n 10970\t  3. Filing and the evidence in view split their inputs. The previous conclusion carries figures without provenance.\n 10971\t  4. Opening's bands amplify an error.\n 10972\t- **Measured:**\n 10973\t  - Data Center Q4 above company Q4 on at least 13 of 26 days in old-1;\n 10974\t  - Data Center's full year above the total's on 20 consecutive days in old-2;\n 10975\t  - different Q3 bases on 17 of 18 paired days;\n 10976\t  - shared evidence between total and Data Center 8% in old-2;\n 10977\t  - 17 of the 24 double-rejected answers from unchecked arithmetic.\n 10978\t- **Recommended design** (a new judge version, Alex's to open):\n 10979\t  - one judging call per related family, each question keeping its answer from one calculation;\n 10980\t  - figures labelled by the judge (source, calculation, assumption; scope and period);\n 10981\t  - code checks only identity and arithmetic (figure in quote, recompute, part within whole, one value per shared quantity, a sourced\n 10982\t    reference);\n 10983\t  - unreconciled forecasts shown as unresolved;\n 10984\t  - extraction unchanged;\n 10985\t  - families declared for the test.\n 10986\t- **Interim for a first release:** number questions shown as \"Forecast unavailable\" until they pass the checks.\n 10987\t- **The test:** a $0 gate (hand reconstructions of five stored cases, four gold controls, three planted errors), then a paid gate\n 10988\t  (36 calls; joint against separate on the three draws' 09-20 pair, plus O, S and E singletons). Pass and stop lines are in `RESULT.md`.\n 10989\t- **Not done:** nothing built, sent or changed.\n 10990\t\n 10991\t## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n 10992\t\n 10993\t- **The questions** (after D725):\n 10994\t  - \"要不要开一个新的判官版本来试修法（相关的题合在一次里算，每个数字标明出处，程序检查算术和出处）？\" Options: 开，先做 0 元那一关\n 10995\t    (recommended: the format and checks designed and through the council, then the $0 gate on five stored cases, four gold controls and\n 10996\t    three planted errors; the paid gate asks Alex for its ceiling); 先不开.\n 10997\t  - \"第一版上线前的过渡：数字题只显示问题和来源，档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'，等通过检查再放出来。你同意这个做法吗？\" Options: 同意\n 10998\t    (recommended); 暂不定.\n 10999\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \"开，先做 0 元那一关 (推荐)\"; \"同意 (推荐)\".\n 11000\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11001\t  - A new judge version is opened for the bounded test of D725: related number questions judged together, with labelled figures and\n 11002\t    code checks of identity and arithmetic. It is designed and reviewed at $0, then the $0 gate runs. The paid gate needs Alex's\n 11003\t    ceiling.\n 11346\t## D741 · 2026-11-22 · Alex rules the three reader questions of D740\n 11347\t\n 11348\t- **The questions** (after D740), each with its options; the recommended option is listed first:\n 11349\t  - 【增速参考】\"写手用公司指引的三季度 1080 亿算出“指引隐含增速约 12%”，参考它定四季度增速 13%，再套在自己预测的三季度 1136 亿上。进入收入计算的三季度数只有 1136 亿这一个。这算不算“同一季度用了两个数”的错？\" Options: 不算错 (推荐); 算错.\n 11350\t  - 【市场参照】\"分析师预期公司全年总收入 4110 亿，最近一个季度数据中心占 92.5%，乘出来约 3800 亿。能不能把这 3800 亿叫作“市场对数据中心全年的预期”？\" Options: 不能 (推荐); 能.\n 11351\t  - 【总开支当数据中心开支】\"问题问四大云厂商“数据中心资本开支”，原文只给了“总资本开支”（并说大部分投向 AI 基础设施）。一份答案直接拿总开支当数据中心开支，没扣非数据中心的部分。可以吗？\" Options: 必须写明扣多少 (推荐); 可以直接用.\n 11352\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \"不算错 (推荐)\"; \"不能 (推荐)\"; \"必须写明扣多少 (推荐)\".\n 11353\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11354\t  1. **Not a defect:** a growth rate computed from guidance and used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate, when one figure\n 11355\t     supplies the quarter in the revenue calculation.\n 11356\t  2. **Not the market's reference:** consensus for a total × a past quarter's reported share. That figure is our comparison estimate.\n 11357\t     Only an outside figure for the member's own quantity (for example Morningstar's direct segment estimate), or a calculation that\n 11358\t     carries no past period's reported share or multiple to another period, is the market's reference.\n 11359\t  3. **A total used for a narrower quantity** (total capex for data-center capex) must state the deduction as its own figure, or give\n 11360\t     a supported bound that shows where the narrower quantity lands.\n 11361\t- **How they are applied (D738):**\n 11362\t  - Ruling 2's carried share is structural, so S5 refuses it.\n 11363\t  - Rulings 1 and 3 go in the request and in the reader brief, because they turn on what a label or an estimate means.\n 11364\t  - Then three steps:\n 11365\t    1. fix the S1 \"from … to …\" range (D740);\n 11366\t    2. check that both reader families apply the rulings the same way to the stored boundary replies;\n 11367\t    3. re-run the registered blind test once with fresh writers and readers.\n 11368\t\n 11369\t## D742 · 2026-11-22 · The v13s re-run stops on one sound answer refused by S4; council 56–56c keeps S4 and makes the request state one benchmark rule; a third $0 blind run follows\n 11370\t\n 11371\t- **The result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND2-RESULT.md`, run `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/`):\n 11372\t  - **STOP on one confirmed registered line.** S4 refused P-v4's Claude writer, whose Q4 = apply_growth(own Q3 $112.5B, growth(Q2\n 11373\t    $96.2B, Q3 guidance $108B)).\n 11374\t    - Both refusal reviewers marked the condition stated and the answer right.\n 11375\t    - Both readers and both adjudicators called the forecast supported.\n 11376\t  - **Every other line passes:**\n 11377\t    - 12 of 12 schema-valid, 11 of 12 accepted;\n 11378\t    - every case usable;\n 11379\t    - the joint case supported in one reply;\n 11380\t    - no settled defect: 5 marks jointly rejected, 9 split, 0 jointly upheld.\n 11381\t  - **Two reader splits, disclosed, not stops:**\n 11382\t    - O's \"$18 billion committed … for the remainder of its fiscal year\" read as part of the $25B balance paid by year-end. It decides\n 11383\t      O's rung, and D741 ruling 2 does not settle it.\n 11384\t    - Wrong numbers in prose that no figure carries (R03, R09, R11). The registered defect types cover figures only.\n 11385\t- **The mechanism.** The request pulled three ways, and the writer followed the system text:\n 11386\t  - the system text: \"a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward\";\n 11387\t  - the schema: a benchmark \"for an estimate\";\n 11388\t  - the header: every path through the forecast.\n 11389\t  S4 matches Alex's ruling 1 as written (\"used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate\").\n 11390\t- **The council rounds:**\n 11391\t  - Round 56 (`codex-r56.md`) confirmed the STOP. It rejected Claude's blanket stop at any % or x figure: a reply building Q4 on the\n 11392\t    guided $108B through a multiple applied twice to Q2 would publish beside Q3 = $112.5B.\n 11393\t  - Round 56b (`codex-r56b.md`) rejected a narrowed `apply_growth` exemption. Arithmetic can pull the forecast back to guidance inside\n 11394\t    the base, and equivalent forms landed on opposite sides of the line.\n 11395\t  - Round 56c (`codex-r56c.md`) chose to keep S4, to state one rule in the request, and to register the refusal review's two judgements\n 11396\t    up front.\n 11397\t- **Decided (council, under Alex's \"那你自己持续迭代\" and D741 ruling 1):**\n 11398\t  1. **S4 is unchanged.**\n 11399\t  2. **The request states one rule** in the system text, the schema and the header:\n 11400\t     - guidance informs the pace;\n 11484\t## D745 · 2026-11-23 · The D744 re-read calibrates the readers but stops on a qualifier-list gap and on S's unsupported share; council 59 recommends a targeted $0 test of one clarification, for Alex to authorize\n 11485\t\n 11486\t- **The result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md` §5; `REREAD2-TALLY.json`):\n 11487\t  - **The readers are calibrated.**\n 11488\t    - All five controls passed: midpoint, 108.5 misread, overlap, disjoint, unsupported assumption.\n 11489\t    - No defect was marked by both readers on the 12 replies.\n 11490\t  - **STOP on two lines, as written:**\n 11491\t    1. T10 (S, Claude writer) F11: \"an estimated $750 billion\" recorded with qualifier \"none\". Both adjudicators upheld it. \"estimated\" is\n 11492\t       not in the closed qualifier list, so the format forced \"none\". This is 1 affected figure of 251 source figures in the three writer\n 11493\t       runs.\n 11494\t    2. S has zero usable replies. Both writers state a data-center share of total capex (90%; 95–100%) that the passages do not size, and\n 11495\t       the share decides the band.\n 11496\t  - **E's Codex reply** is now \"not supported\": its 15% cut from the guided floor decides the band. This is the same weakness.\n 11497\t- **Council round 59** (`codex-r59.md`) chose a targeted $0 test, (c), over Claude's lean to go to Alex for the paid re-send, (b):\n 11498\t  - Going straight to the paid re-send would measure the known weakness in gpt-6-luna without the request saying what a supported size\n 11499\t    is.\n 11500\t  - Skipping a clean result needs Alex to change the registered sequence anyway.\n 11501\t  - Claude agrees: the weakness is unsupported precision in a number that decides the rung, which is the goal's own failure (D725).\n 11502\t- **Proposed test (for Alex to authorize):**\n 11503\t  1. Add \"estimated\" to the qualifier list, and show readers the allowed values. Prove it on the saved replies, with a case and a\n 11504\t     mutant.\n 11505\t  2. Add one clarification to the existing instruction: when a deduction or cut decides the band, show the evidence for its size or a\n 11506\t     bound the passages support that justifies the band; if neither, answer unresolved.\n 11507\t  3. Test on S and on one stored case where the passages do support a narrower figure.\n 11508\t  4. Before the test, Alex rules whether a justified unresolved answer counts as usable.\n 11509\t  - Falsifier: a fresh S answer still picks a band on an unsupported share, or the supported case is withheld.\n 11510\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-23):\n 11511\t  - to \"怎么走？\": \"批准针对性小测 (推荐)\". The other options were \"不小测，直接议花钱重发\" and \"先停在这里\".\n 11512\t  - to whether a justified \"无法判断\" counts: \"算合格 (推荐)\". The other option was \"不算\".\n 11513\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11514\t  1. Run the targeted $0 test.\n 11515\t  2. An unresolved answer whose reason shows the passages cannot settle the rung counts as a usable answer.\n 11516\t- **Council round 60** (`codex-r60.md`) set the wording and the registration (`SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D745]):\n 11517\t  - Rung-deciding shares, deductions and discounts must show their passage support or a justifying bound, else unresolved.\n 11518\t  - The default discount is made subject to that rule.\n 11519\t  - The three controls are the saved E 15% cut, a vague P-v8 unresolved answer and a justified S unresolved answer (expected no, no,\n 11520\t    yes).\n 11521\t  - Pass: every S and E reply settled yes on a forecast or its reason; both P-v8 replies settled yes on a forecast. A support split\n 11522\t    is inconclusive.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
