{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/REREAD2-TALLY.json | sed -n '90,205p'; nl -ba poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/reread2-packets/T15.codex.json; nl -ba poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/reread2-packets/T15.claude.json\"","aggregated_output":"    90\t ],\n    91\t \"split_marks\": [],\n    92\t \"support\": {\n    93\t  \"T02 O/claude v29\": [\n    94\t   \"split\",\n    95\t   [\n    96\t    \"no\",\n    97\t    \"yes\",\n    98\t    \"no\",\n    99\t    \"yes\"\n   100\t   ]\n   101\t  ],\n   102\t  \"T04 P/codex v4\": [\n   103\t   \"yes\",\n   104\t   [\n   105\t    \"yes\",\n   106\t    \"yes\"\n   107\t   ]\n   108\t  ],\n   109\t  \"T04 P/codex v8\": [\n   110\t   \"yes\",\n   111\t   [\n   112\t    \"yes\",\n   113\t    \"yes\"\n   114\t   ]\n   115\t  ],\n   116\t  \"T05 P-v8/claude v8\": [\n   117\t   \"yes\",\n   118\t   [\n   119\t    \"yes\",\n   120\t    \"yes\"\n   121\t   ]\n   122\t  ],\n   123\t  \"T06 S/codex v6\": [\n   124\t   \"no\",\n   125\t   [\n   126\t    \"no\",\n   127\t    \"no\"\n   128\t   ]\n   129\t  ],\n   130\t  \"T07 P-v4/codex v4\": [\n   131\t   \"yes\",\n   132\t   [\n   133\t    \"yes\",\n   134\t    \"yes\"\n   135\t   ]\n   136\t  ],\n   137\t  \"T09 P-v4/claude v4\": [\n   138\t   \"yes\",\n   139\t   [\n   140\t    \"yes\",\n   141\t    \"yes\"\n   142\t   ]\n   143\t  ],\n   144\t  \"T10 S/claude v6\": [\n   145\t   \"split\",\n   146\t   [\n   147\t    \"no\",\n   148\t    \"yes\",\n   149\t    \"no\",\n   150\t    \"yes\"\n   151\t   ]\n   152\t  ],\n   153\t  \"T11 P-v8/codex v8\": [\n   154\t   \"yes\",\n   155\t   [\n   156\t    \"yes\",\n   157\t    \"yes\"\n   158\t   ]\n   159\t  ],\n   160\t  \"T12 O/codex v29\": [\n   161\t   \"yes\",\n   162\t   [\n   163\t    \"no\",\n   164\t    \"yes\",\n   165\t    \"yes\",\n   166\t    \"yes\"\n   167\t   ]\n   168\t  ],\n   169\t  \"T15 E/claude v41\": [\n   170\t   \"yes\",\n   171\t   [\n   172\t    \"yes\",\n   173\t    \"yes\"\n   174\t   ]\n   175\t  ],\n   176\t  \"T16 P/claude v4\": [\n   177\t   \"yes\",\n   178\t   [\n   179\t    \"yes\",\n   180\t    \"yes\"\n   181\t   ]\n   182\t  ],\n   183\t  \"T16 P/claude v8\": [\n   184\t   \"yes\",\n   185\t   [\n   186\t    \"yes\",\n   187\t    \"yes\"\n   188\t   ]\n   189\t  ],\n   190\t  \"T17 E/codex v41\": [\n   191\t   \"no\",\n   192\t   [\n   193\t    \"no\",\n   194\t    \"no\"\n   195\t   ]\n   196\t  ]\n   197\t },\n   198\t \"usable\": {\n   199\t  \"O\": [\n   200\t   \"codex\"\n   201\t  ],\n   202\t  \"P\": [\n   203\t   \"codex\",\n   204\t   \"claude\"\n   205\t  ],\n     1\t{\n     2\t  \"members\": {\n     3\t    \"v41\": {\n     4\t      \"supported\": \"yes\",\n     5\t      \"ground\": \"The forecast applies an estimated 85% growth rate to the $20 billion FY2027 base (e3660, e4856), yielding $37 billion in rung 3. NVIDIA's doubling outlook (e4691, e4856) anchors the estimate. Broad planned deployments (e4689) support growth above the outside market benchmarks (e4687, e4857). Anthropic's evaluation (e5044) gives no order volume, and AMD's benchmark claims (e5399, e5400, e5401, e5402, e5404) support allowing for competition as Vera ramps.\",\n     6\t      \"why_not\": \"\"\n     7\t    }\n     8\t  },\n     9\t  \"defects\": []\n    10\t}     1\t{\"members\": {\"v41\": {\"supported\": \"yes\", \"ground\": \"F8 = apply_growth(F1 $20bn FY2027 CPU revenue from e3660, F7 85%) = 37, rung 3 ($30-40bn). The band rests on F7's stated assumption: management's 'more than double' (F2, e4856; repeated in e4691, e4764) is discounted for time and execution because it is a full next-fiscal-year target for a product still ramping, with no volume shown in hand (e4689 says Vera 'will be deployed'; e5044 says Anthropic is only evaluating it). The size of the discount is argued from the outside market pace of about 50% a year (e4687; e4857's $35bn to $170bn, about 48% a year), so a doubling needs large share gains, and from AMD's competitive benchmark claims against Vera (e5399, e5400, e5401, e5402, e5404); the adoption breadth (e4689, e5044, e4692) is weighed the other way. The system text sanctions discounting a target with no volume in hand, and any discount below 2x puts the outcome in rung 3, so the band is checkable against the passages; the exact 85% is the writer's judgement. Equating the FY2027 $20bn CPU figure and the doubling with Vera CPU revenue rests on e4856's and e4691's passages, which tie both to Vera, and is stated in reasons. One loose sentence: the move condition 'if FY2027 lands at or above $20 billion' would not change a forecast that already assumes a $20bn base.\", \"why_not\": \"\"}}, \"defects\": []}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
