{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/TALLY.json | head -125; rg -n 'coverage|gain|usable|separate' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md | tail -30\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t{\n     2\t \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n     3\t \"lines\": [\n     4\t  \"U01 P-v8  K-unresolved-unjustified  v8 unresolved settled=no     votes=['no', 'no'] [control expects no] ok\",\n     5\t  \"U02 S     claude                    v6 forecast   settled=split  votes=['no', 'yes', 'no', 'yes'] [a supported forecast or a justified unresolved answer] MISS\",\n     6\t  \"U03 E     K-unsupported             v41 forecast   settled=no     votes=['no', 'no'] [control expects no] ok\",\n     7\t  \"U04 S     K-unresolved-justified    v6 unresolved settled=split  votes=['yes', 'no', 'yes', 'no'] [control expects yes] MISS\",\n     8\t  \"U05 E     codex                     v41 forecast   settled=no     votes=['no', 'no'] [a supported forecast or a justified unresolved answer] MISS\",\n     9\t  \"U06 E     claude                    v41 forecast   settled=split  votes=['no', 'yes', 'no', 'yes'] [a supported forecast or a justified unresolved answer] MISS\",\n    10\t  \"U07 P-v8  codex                     v8 forecast   settled=yes    votes=['yes', 'yes'] [a supported forecast] ok\",\n    11\t  \"U08 S     codex                     v6 forecast   settled=split  votes=['no', 'yes', 'no', 'yes'] [a supported forecast or a justified unresolved answer] MISS\",\n    12\t  \"U09 P-v8  claude                    v8 forecast   settled=yes    votes=['yes', 'yes'] [a supported forecast] ok\"\n    13\t ],\n    14\t \"settled_defects\": [],\n    15\t \"split_defects\": [],\n    16\t \"refused\": []\n    17\t}17:- **Every case has a usable reply.** The joint case has both forecasts supported in one reply (R02 and R11).\n47:  - e1947: more than $730B \"on AI infrastructure\" against $720–745B of capex;\n51:  This is not a registered stop line (usable is counted per case, and S has R01). It is a real judgement error in an answer that would\n53:- **R06 (O, Claude writer) is split again** on the $18B reading: Codex says not supported, Claude says supported. This is the same\n67:  - R01, the only usable S reply, marks Zacks's $720–745B of *total* capex as the market reference for *data-center* capex. Claude's\n69:  - R11's prose offers \"$138 billion in Q4\" as reaching rung 1, but it gives $428.32B against the $431.2B edge. The forecast itself\n84:- **STOP again, as written: Q10 (P-v8, Codex writer).**\n99:  - O's Claude reply (Q09) is split again.\n116:  2. **A case with zero usable first replies: S.**\n127:  - O's Codex reply is supported after adjudication; O's Claude reply is split again.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '11397,11412p' ; nl -ba poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/E/schema.json | sed -n '205,232p;285,336p'\"","aggregated_output":" 11397\t- **Decided (council, under Alex's \"那你自己持续迭代\" and D741 ruling 1):**\n 11398\t  1. **S4 is unchanged.**\n 11399\t  2. **The request states one rule** in the system text, the schema and the header:\n 11400\t     - guidance informs the pace;\n 11401\t     - the forecast pace is recorded as an estimate naming its benchmark in `rests_on`;\n 11402\t     - the quarter's dollar value is the one forecast figure;\n 11403\t     - the header says the first figure of a shared quantity reached on every arithmetic path, through rates and multiples too, is its\n 11404\t       forecast.\n 11405\t  3. **The readers' brief and the adjudication header** keep Alex's sentence and add: look through any rate or multiple, including\n 11406\t     inside a stated assumption, for a second dollar value. The adjudication packet now includes the system text.\n 11407\t  4. **The refusal review** records \"sound\" and \"stated\" apart. A sound answer refused under a clearly stated condition still stops.\n 11408\t     The stop lines are unchanged (`SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D742]).\n 11409\t  5. **Part A:** cases 109 of 109 (5 new); mutants 42 of 42 (1 new); rehearsal 19 of 19. The v13 plan hash is unchanged (6f81dae5…),\n 11410\t     and the v13s plan changes as intended.\n 11411\t  6. **`s4_replay.py` on the saved reply.** The reply as written and both council resets are refused. The stated-estimate form passes\n 11412\t     at $416.62B.\n   205\t      ]\n   206\t     },\n   207\t     \"basis_text\": {\n   208\t      \"anyOf\": [\n   209\t       {\n   210\t        \"type\": \"string\",\n   211\t        \"description\": \"Estimate only: the assumption, in words.\"\n   212\t       },\n   213\t       {\n   214\t        \"type\": \"null\"\n   215\t       }\n   216\t      ]\n   217\t     },\n   218\t     \"rests_on\": {\n   219\t      \"anyOf\": [\n   220\t       {\n   221\t        \"type\": \"array\",\n   222\t        \"items\": {\n   223\t         \"type\": \"string\"\n   224\t        },\n   225\t        \"description\": \"Estimate only: the ids of the figures and passages it rests on.\"\n   226\t       },\n   227\t       {\n   228\t        \"type\": \"null\"\n   229\t       }\n   230\t      ]\n   231\t     },\n   232\t     \"outcome_for\": {\n   285\t      ]\n   286\t     },\n   287\t     \"shape\": {\n   288\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n   289\t      \"enum\": [\n   290\t       \"forecast\",\n   291\t       \"unresolved\"\n   292\t      ],\n   293\t      \"description\": \"forecast: a figure marked in outcome_for, a rung, and a reference (a figure marked in reference_for, or reference_unavailable). unresolved: why; rung and reference_unavailable null; no figure marked for it.\"\n   294\t     },\n   295\t     \"rung\": {\n   296\t      \"anyOf\": [\n   297\t       {\n   298\t        \"type\": \"integer\",\n   299\t        \"description\": \"Forecast only: the rung whose band holds the outcome as the code recomputes it (a band includes its lower edge, not its upper); for a range outcome, a band it overlaps, with the reason in reasons.\"\n   300\t       },\n   301\t       {\n   302\t        \"type\": \"null\"\n   303\t       }\n   304\t      ]\n   305\t     },\n   306\t     \"reference_unavailable\": {\n   307\t      \"anyOf\": [\n   308\t       {\n   309\t        \"type\": \"string\",\n   310\t        \"description\": \"Forecast only, when no figure is marked as its reference: why.\"\n   311\t       },\n   312\t       {\n   313\t        \"type\": \"null\"\n   314\t       }\n   315\t      ]\n   316\t     },\n   317\t     \"reasons\": {\n   318\t      \"type\": \"string\"\n   319\t     },\n   320\t     \"why\": {\n   321\t      \"anyOf\": [\n   322\t       {\n   323\t        \"type\": \"string\",\n   324\t        \"description\": \"Unresolved only: why the evidence cannot support a forecast.\"\n   325\t       },\n   326\t       {\n   327\t        \"type\": \"null\"\n   328\t       }\n   329\t      ]\n   330\t     },\n   331\t     \"cites\": {\n   332\t      \"type\": \"array\",\n   333\t      \"items\": {\n   334\t       \"type\": \"string\",\n   335\t       \"enum\": [\n   336\t        \"e3660\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'attainable|before.*run|could.*change' AGENTS.md; nl -ba poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/controls/K-unresolved-justified.json | rg 'why' | cut -c1-1500; nl -ba poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/reread2-packets/T10.codex.json | head -25; nl -ba poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/reread2-packets/T10.claude.json | cut -c1-1800\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'attainable|before.*run|could.*change' AGENTS.md; nl -ba poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/controls/K-unresolved-justified.json | rg 'why' | cut -c1-1500; nl -ba poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/reread2-packets/T10.codex.json | head -25; nl -ba poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/reread2-packets/T10.claude.json | cut -c1-1800\"","aggregated_output":"86:- A failure called a flake is a defect until traced. Read a failing check to its first differing line before any rerun; a passing rerun\n155:- Write the one decisive assertion that fails without the code under test, and predict the run before running it. A first failure for\n186:  diagnosed before the run; a paid run is never the way a check or a prompt is first tried.\n231:- **Check before the send, at no cost.** Write one answer that follows the prompt and run every code check on it: a request never asks\n357:  analysis stability test. This is a principle you should remember\"). A day or week slice before any whole-corpus run; preflight on\n358:  stored data before any paid run (§5); no edit while a run is live (§9). A paid run measures a configuration; it never tries a fix.\n     1\t{\"figures\": [{\"id\": \"F1\", \"what\": {\"population\": \"four largest AI hyperscalers\", \"measure\": \"total capital expenditure\", \"scope\": \"combined\", \"period\": \"CY2026\"}, \"kind\": \"source\", \"basis\": \"third_party\", \"value\": null, \"low\": 720, \"high\": 745, \"unit\": \"USD bn\", \"evidence_id\": \"e5014\", \"quote_number\": \"$720 billion to $745 billion\", \"qualifier\": \"roughly\", \"inputs\": null, \"operation\": null, \"basis_text\": null, \"rests_on\": null, \"outcome_for\": [], \"reference_for\": []}, {\"id\": \"F2\", \"what\": {\"population\": \"four largest AI hyperscalers\", \"measure\": \"total capital expenditure\", \"scope\": \"combined\", \"period\": \"CY2026\"}, \"kind\": \"source\", \"basis\": \"third_party\", \"value\": 760, \"low\": null, \"high\": null, \"unit\": \"USD bn\", \"evidence_id\": \"e2458\", \"quote_number\": \"$760 billion\", \"qualifier\": \"none\", \"inputs\": null, \"operation\": null, \"basis_text\": null, \"rests_on\": null, \"outcome_for\": [], \"reference_for\": []}, {\"id\": \"F3\", \"what\": {\"population\": \"Alphabet\", \"measure\": \"total capital expenditure\", \"scope\": \"company-wide\", \"period\": \"CY2026\"}, \"kind\": \"source\", \"basis\": \"guidance\", \"value\": null, \"low\": 195, \"high\": 205, \"unit\": \"USD bn\", \"evidence_id\": \"e1254\", \"quote_number\": \"$195 billion to $205 billion\", \"qualifier\": \"none\", \"inputs\": null, \"operation\": null, \"basis_text\": null, \"rests_on\": null, \"outcome_for\": [], \"reference_for\": []}, {\"id\": \"F4\", \"what\": {\"population\": \"Amazon\", \"measure\": \"total capital expenditure\", \"scope\": \"company-wide\", \"period\": \"CY2026\"}, \"kind\": \n     1\t{\n     2\t  \"members\": {\n     3\t    \"v6\": {\n     4\t      \"supported\": \"no\",\n     5\t      \"ground\": \"F6 estimates $175 billion in Microsoft capital expenditure using e922, e4405 and outside estimates of the four companies’ total spending. F13 assumes 95–100% of combined capital expenditure goes to data centers, citing e1649, e5014, e1416, e4082 and e5376. That yields $679.25–745 billion, with a midpoint of $712.125 billion in rung 4.\",\n     6\t      \"why_not\": \"The passages support substantial data-center spending, but they do not establish that other spending accounts for at most 5% of the four companies’ combined capital expenditure. e1649 explains Amazon’s increase, and e5014 says a large portion goes to AI infrastructure without sizing it. The data-center estimates cover a broader or unspecified group. F8 is an outside estimate of total capital expenditure, so it does not independently show what the market expects for the data-center portion.\"\n     7\t    }\n     8\t  },\n     9\t  \"defects\": [\n    10\t    {\n    11\t      \"type\": \"number misread\",\n    12\t      \"figures\": [\"F11\"],\n    13\t      \"detail\": \"e1416 says “an estimated $750 billion.” F11 gives the correct amount but omits the qualifier.\"\n    14\t    }\n    15\t  ]\n    16\t}     1\t{\"members\": {\"v6\": {\"supported\": \"yes\", \"ground\": \"Build of the four companies' 2026 capital expenditure from the shown guidance: Alphabet $195-205bn (e1254, F1), Meta $125-145bn (e1549, F2), Amazon $220bn (e1649, F3), plus a stated estimate for Microsoft of $175bn (F6), set between a run-rate build from its January-March 2026 quarter of $30.88bn up 84% (e922; 15% sequential growth gives about $154bn, checked) and the residual of the outside four-company tallies (e5014 $720-745bn, e1856 $745bn, e2458 $760bn) less the other three companies' guidance ($540-570bn); combined $715-745bn (F7, sum checked). The stated 95-100% data-center share (F13) rests on outside sources labelling the same totals as data-center spending (NVIDIA's top-five nearly $800bn is called capex in e2759 and data-center capex in e4766/e5376; e4082 around $750bn of AI data-center spending); share gives $679.25-745bn (F14, checked), midpoint about $712bn, rung 4 chosen as a band the range overlaps with the reason given. Reference e5014 ($720-745bn, four companies) also sits in rung 4. A reader can check every step; the rung-4 call leans on two stated assumptions (Microsoft at $175bn rather than the ~$155bn run-rate, and a near-total data-center share, against e5014's weaker 'large portion'), and the basis text's '$175-190bn at their centres' understates the top of the residual range (the $760bn tally gives about $205bn), which does not weaken the chosen value.\", \"why_not\": \"\"}}, \"defects\": []}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"agent_message","text":"The saved Vera answers show why the paid result is still open. Two readers rejected the $36B forecast, but the paid test asks a separate question about whether an unsupported adjustment decided the band. I also found that the proposed re-read lists the same spending control twice."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'E\\\\b|discount|unresolved|reference' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r60.md | head -22; rg -n 'D737|re-send|paid re-send' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -35\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'E\\\\b|discount|unresolved|reference' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r60.md | head -22; rg -n 'D737|re-send|paid re-send' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -35\"","aggregated_output":"3:1. **Serious — Say what must support the estimate, and qualify “discounted by default.”** The proposed sentence is general and captures when to leave an answer unresolved. Council 59 also requires the writer to **show** what supports the amount or the bound. “One estimate” can miss a calculation where several adjustments together decide the band. And the default discount gives a reason to expect a cut, while leaving its size open. E’s saved $34B answer shows what happens when the writer fills in that gap with a 15% cut. Keep the discount principle and make it subject to the closing evidence requirement. Replace the existing unresolved sentence with:\n5:   > If the chosen rung depends on a share, deduction or discount, show what in the passages supports its size or gives a bound that justifies the rung. If the evidence cannot support a forecast, answer unresolved and explain the gap.\n7:   At the earlier instruction, change “is discounted by default” to “is discounted subject to the evidence requirement below.” Keep the condition for taking the target in full. This preserves the existing discount principle and makes clear what it can justify. [Current instructions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt:4) · [E’s 85% realization estimate](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/E/answers/codex.json:75) · [D745 and Alex’s answers](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11502)\n11:3. **Serious — Test both reader errors.** The 140% E control is valid for spotting an unsupported forecast. The saved $34B E answer is a sharper replacement because its unsupported cut is the exact failure under review. Keep the P-v8 vague unresolved control and add a **justified unresolved S** control. Its reason should explain why the four companies’ total capex, their AI infrastructure spending, and five companies’ data-center capex cannot settle the four-company data-center band. Expect **no, no, yes**, respectively. I checked both E negatives and both unresolved forms in memory. All passed the schema and code checks, so the readers’ verdicts are what distinguish them. Update the first-reader instructions and adjudication together. For a forecast, ask what evidence supports the assumption that decides the band. For an unresolved answer, ask what gap remains after reading the strongest relevant passages. The current first-reader form asks only what puts a forecast in its band. [Existing E control](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_reread2.py:74) · [S spending passages](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/S/user.txt:75) · [First-reader instructions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_reread2.py:22) · [Adjudication instructions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_adjudicate.py:21) · [Unresolved answer check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:185)\n13:4. **Serious — Register exactly what earns the paid re-send request.** D745’s written test names S and one supported case. It also names E as the same failure. Resolve that difference explicitly when registering the proposed six-writer scope. With E included, require six unedited first replies, nine blinded packets including the three controls, and 18 first readings plus any adjudications. The existing inventory expects all six historical cases, and the old control builder requires joint P. Register the smaller inventory explicitly. Every S and E reply needs a settled **yes** on either a forecast or its reason for leaving the answer unresolved. Both P-v8 replies need a settled **yes** on a forecast. A remaining support split leaves the run inconclusive and sends it back to council. Keep the existing refusal and defect stops. A clean result supports asking Alex to authorize the 36-request re-send, which is where the production model is measured. [D745 scope](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11494) · [Existing inventory](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_test.py:118) · [Existing control builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_reread2.py:54) · [Registered stops and paid sequence](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:267)\n2620:- Found in the three-month resume (`english-v34-nvda-3m-2026-10-28`, 01:32): the judgement of v10 (Data Center revenue, a 24,150-token request) came back empty with `finish_reason` length: all 8,000 completion tokens were reasoning tokens, so the code read a malformed answer and the day halted (resumable; the re-send passed). Census over every archive: 2 of 793 judge answers hit the cap this way (the other in `english-v29-nvda-3m`, a 56k-token request), 13 of 793 used 6,000 or more. The archive books such a call at $0 while it costs its tokens (about $0.006 each).\n2695:  over seven articles, at least one per draw (v21: one in ten, erased by the re-send); the ACP amount question 3/3; about 10 of 25\n2697:  Acceptance (`english-v38-nvda-1w-2026-10-28`, $0.23, drops read one by one): 98 sends for 98 items, no re-send; every story of the week\n2991:- Decided: when (and only when) the architecture is adopted after the measurement in design.md, the open-question list an extraction request shows is a snapshot frozen once per day; every article of that day sees the same list; the archive key is (item, snapshot hash); a day in flight never re-sends an item because the ledger moved. This narrows D211 (\"the request depends on the item alone\") to \"depends on the item and the day's snapshot\". Not decided: whether other companies' questions are shown, whether the one-home rule (D207) moves into the extraction prompt, what happens to a failed candidate's evidence; the measurement's predictions P1–P6 are frozen in design.md (sha256 in `predictions.sha256`).\n3009:- Decided: the takes line is the one rule for what a question's file holds; the system prompt (`placement-narrow-v4`, 1,311 characters against v2's 1,587) says only how to apply it: narrowest covering question, that one only; a covered statement belongs in the file whoever says it (the company, a named analyst or bank, a customer, a competitor, a reporter) and with or without a period, basis or exact amount, the weight being the judge's; the period in a takes line tells questions apart and bars no driver from another period when no open question covers it; nothing a takes line covers is filed under none. D207's \"only their own\" sentence goes: an analyst betting on a company's revenue reads every credible estimate of it, and the signed standard keeps third-party estimates as core (gold v5: SemiAnalysis, Morgan Stanley). The anti-sink gate D207 wanted is the takes line's own \"direct drivers of that figure stated with a size\" plus the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions (D253 seeds); the 2026-10-31 stored re-send showed that removing the \"only their own\" sentence filed 11 more gold homes and no more noise. The event takes line (`placement.takes()`) now also names \"cancellations, design or configuration changes\", the content of a v2 sentence the proof showed the takes line lacked (a scrapped alternative rack plan 2/3 → 0/3 without it); the catch-all measure `other` is no longer printed as a word.\n3054:- Proof (`proof-judging-v6.txt`, `proof-judging-v6b.txt`: the last stored judgement request of 14 theses of arm 4 draw 1 re-sent once each under v6 and read beside the stored v5 answers, about a cent): every answer names the reference and derives the implied outcome. Six rungs moved against the stored ones: non-GAAP gross margin 3 → 2 (Q1 reported 75% and Q2 guided 75% sit on the rung-2 boundary), 2027 hyperscaler capex 4 → 5 (management's own \"more than $1 trillion\"), China accelerator share 4 → 5 (share \"fallen to zero\"), China H200 authorization No → Yes (a reported plan to permit named firms and reported progress in reviews, six months before the deadline), Data Center revenue 2 → 3 ($355–360 billion derived from Q1 and the total-revenue proxy, below the $360 billion boundary), Blackwell+Rubin revenue 2 → 1 in the first send by annualising a two-year \"$1 trillion visibility\" figure to $545 billion, a part above its whole: clause (3)'s consistency check was added for it and the re-send gives rung 2 ($320–360 billion, a share of the Data Center segment). Total revenue stays at 3 with the arithmetic shown (H1 $172.6 billion from Q1 and the Q2 guide; $400 billion needs more than $227 billion in H2). Prompt 2,453 → 3,782 characters: the request defined neither what a rung means nor a reference and its \"established\" wording forced the defect; the two sentences that carried it were cut. Configuration `poc-v90` (poc-v89 with judging-v6); the default stays `poc-v69`. Tests: `tests/test_stance_fields.py`. Measured by re-sent stored requests, not by an arm (Alex: \"不要再跑这些有的没的臂了\").\n3134:- Measured (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/design-v78-fields.md` §12; three sets, 50 stored articles, three sends each against v94's three stored draws, one round): gold matters reaching 132 → 146; gold not-kept statements reaching 95 → 89, and 71 → 56 once records whose long quote also carries a kept matter are set apart (D250 item 5). On the way, v74b (95 → 77 noise) lost a core matter in all three sends (a partner's disclosed backstop amount): my sentence on \"the results a user reports from that use\" contradicted kind 2's reported figures, and the new quote-copy wording dropped the partner figure out of the programme's record; the model's own account (`probe-v101-omitted.txt`) and two cheap re-sends located and fixed both (v74c, v74d).\n3530:- The [development study](research/2026-10-27-extraction-stability/plan.md) uses the admission-v12 worktree's runtime and three preserved benchmark articles. It crosses the original versus analyst prompt with original versus reporting-only text, five independent calls per cell, with exact HTTP request bytes preserved. The original property order is reconstructed because the earlier archive's canonical JSON reordered the schema before re-sending it.\n3700:  candidate were judged distinct (\"any\" against \"public\" authorization) in one draw; ten re-sends of the stored request gave the same\n4397:  (code, tests, mutants, the pre-send checks, the request audit) and Stage A is sent, with a spending cap of $3. A line missed stops\n4881:- **Council** (D439; Alex not active): an independent Codex member and Claude argued four rounds (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mj-*`). Agreed facts: gate 2 failed under its declared rules (two stop lines on the memory article); the link line measured the wrong thing (c8's request returns an uncovered statement with empty links); the 3-of-9 against 0-of-9 memory-thesis difference is real and its cause is not established. The council's first position was to keep c8; Claude's was a larger re-send. The consensus, after Claude adopted the council's changes (a margin fixed in advance, a three-way result in which inconclusive is not a pass, retained statements decisive, an exercised-control rule, a named and simulation-validated interval): \"Council position: consensus on the rule in mj-challenge-2.md as amended by mj-challenge-3.md\" (`mj-codex-4.md`).\n7393:## D576 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: Stage B's control line cannot be exercised by re-sending the judge; no delivery check; next, at $0, a census of the unlisted-parts class now that the page reads the list (council consensus, rounds 53 to 58)\n7398:  apart) 4 count; eligibility and the material shown were set before the judge ran, so an unchanged judge-only re-send stays at 4; on\n7650:- **Pre-send checks ($0):**\n7715:## D592 · 2026-11-16 · The final-answer test's control line: an unchanged re-send cannot exercise it, and the 7-control course is not started for the line's sake; the live-service operating contract is resumed as a $0 design (council round 110)\n7718:  - An unchanged judge re-send stays at 4 comparable controls of the 8 needed.\n8908:- **Cost:** Opus is about $0.058 a topic, about 65 times luna and not below astra. It counts about 68% more input tokens. The pre-send\n10104:- **Ran under D679**, for $2.13 of a $5 ledger: 140 c8 sends, 98 judge calls in two arms, 15 noise re-sends, and two blind reader\n10155:  - **J2a (schema order only):** moves the same 2 targets as v7's re-send; the falsifier fired.\n10181:    by the rule. v7's own re-send loses 3 of 24 controls, which is the readers' noise.\n10708:  - No pre-send size rule: an HTTP 400 is the visible stop.\n11163:    - Only then is a re-send of the same 36 requests asked for, under a new decision with D725's lines unchanged.\n11180:  - A clean result goes back to Alex as a request to re-send the same 36 requests under a new decision, with D725's lines\n11199:    Only the paid re-send measures whether luna can follow it.\n11236:## D737 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: shrink judging-v13's format to the checks that stop the named defects, then a $0 blind test\n11242:    become assumptions shown to readers; council, then the $0 blind test, then a request for the paid re-send;\n11254:  - Then the $0 blind test (REPAIR-DESIGN.md §5, with round 51's reader fix). A clean result returns to Alex for the paid re-send under\n11260:- **Rounds 52 and 53** (`research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r52.md`, `codex-r53.md`) reviewed the small format within D737's\n11265:- **Settled (how D737's rule is built; D737 says code refuses only for the five defects, not that code catches every instance):**\n11344:    - re-run the registered blind test once with fresh writers and readers, then the paid re-send request.\n11414:     confirmed to carry two values of a quarter, goes back to council. Only a run meeting every line goes to Alex for the paid re-send.\n11447:  A clean re-read goes to Alex for the paid re-send. Nothing paid before that.\n11482:  stop ends it. A clean result goes to Alex for the paid re-send.\n11497:- **Council round 59** (`codex-r59.md`) chose a targeted $0 test, (c), over Claude's lean to go to Alex for the paid re-send, (b):\n11498:  - Going straight to the paid re-send would measure the known weakness in gpt-6-luna without the request saying what a supported size\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
